<h2>Section 1: Overview and Core Separation from Clinical Health Records</h2>
<p>This Privacy Policy outlines how The Geriatrician&rsquo;s Guide LLC collects, utilizes, secures, and discloses personal data through our website and its integrated educational platforms.</p>
<p><b>This website is a commercial and educational publication platform. It is not a clinical healthcare portal.</b> The Geriatrician&rsquo;s Guide LLC explicitly states that all personal data, tracking metrics, and payment details collected through this website are utilized solely for commercial operations and educational delivery. This data infrastructure is entirely separate, independent, and isolated from protected clinical health records and HIPAA-regulated data systems. No clinical health information is requested, maintained, or stored on this platform. The Websites are not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.</p>

<h2>Section 2: Information Collected by the Company</h2>
<p>We limit data collection to information that is reasonably necessary to provide educational materials, process commercial transactions, and deliver communications. The platform collects the following categories of data:</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Contact Data (via Kit):</b> We collect email addresses provided by users when subscribing to our newsletter, downloading free lead magnets, or accessing gated tools. Our email list and marketing communications are managed securely via our third-party processor, <b>Kit</b> (formerly ConvertKit).</li>
<li><b>Identity Data:</b> First and last names provided voluntarily when downloading materials or completing a purchase.</li>
<li><b>Financial Transaction Data:</b> Credit card details and billing addresses required to complete digital ebook purchases. All financial transactions are transmitted directly via encrypted protocols to our third-party payment processor, Lemon Squeezy, which acts as the Merchant of Record for our digital product sales. The Company does not store raw financial data on its own servers.</li>
<li><b>Technical Tracking Data:</b> We do not currently use cookie-based analytics, advertising, or retargeting tools on the Websites. If we use website analytics now or in the future, we will limit them to privacy-focused, cookieless tools (such as Fathom or Plausible) that may collect Internet protocol (IP) addresses, browser types, and website interaction metrics to monitor and improve website functionality, and we will update this Privacy Policy if our practices change. Our web host may also keep standard server logs. Our third-party service providers (such as Kit and Lemon Squeezy) may use cookies or similar technologies on their own forms, pages, and emails (for example, to confirm that an email was opened), which are governed by their own privacy policies. We do not track your activity over time across other websites, and we do not allow third-party advertising or analytics providers to do so through the Websites, so we do not respond differently to &quot;Do Not Track&quot; browser signals.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Section 3: Interactive Assessment Tool (&quot;Is It Time?&quot;)</h2>
<p>Our platform features an interactive self-assessment tool designed to help families evaluate senior care needs. We have architected this tool with strict privacy-by-design principles:</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Session Storage Only; No Server-Side Storage:</b> The &quot;Is It Time?&quot; tool temporarily utilizes your browser's session storage strictly to prevent data loss if you refresh the page. All inputs are permanently cleared the moment you close your browser tab. We do not use persistent cookies for this tool, and your specific assessment answers are never transmitted to or stored on our servers.</li>
<li>All responses selected during the quiz are processed dynamically in the browser to generate your immediate educational outcome and are permanently discarded when you close your browser tab. We do not track, aggregate, or retain your specific answers regarding your loved one&rsquo;s health or capabilities.</li>
<li>To access the tool's results, you will be required to affirmatively consent to our <a href="/terms">Terms of Use</a> by clicking a required checkbox (clickwrap agreement). If you choose to provide an email address, it is securely routed to our email processor (Kit) to deliver your results and related educational materials, but your specific quiz answers are never tied to this email in our records.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Section 4: Purpose and Utilization of Collected Data</h2>
<p>We process personal data strictly for the following purposes:</p>
<ul>
<li>Fulfilling and delivering commercial orders for digital ebooks and downloads.</li>
<li>Delivering administrative updates, guides, and educational rubrics you have requested.</li>
<li>Sending promotional newsletters and marketing communications via Kit, subject to your explicit right to opt out at any time.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Section 5: Disclosures to Third Parties</h2>
<p>The Geriatrician&rsquo;s Guide LLC does not sell, lease, or trade user data to third-party data brokers. Personal data is shared exclusively with authorized third-party service providers acting as data processors under binding corporate contracts. These include:</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Kit:</b> For the secure processing, segmentation, and delivery of our email newsletters and digital guides.</li>
<li><b>Lemon Squeezy (Merchant of Record):</b> For the secure processing of payments and taxes on our digital product sales. Lemon Squeezy collects and uses your payment information under its own privacy policy.</li>
<li><b>Website Hosting Providers:</b> To maintain the operational functionality of the website.</li>
</ul>
<p>All processors are contractually restricted from using user data for any purpose outside the explicit service boundaries defined by the Company.</p>

<h2>Section 6: Consumer Rights and Opt-Out Framework</h2>
<p>Users possess specific rights regarding their personal data:</p>
<ul>
<li><b>The Right to Access &amp; Deletion:</b> You may request formal confirmation regarding your personal data and request its complete deletion from our marketing platforms, subject to standard legal/financial retention mandates for accounting.</li>
<li><b>The Right to Opt-Out:</b> You retain the absolute right to opt out of marketing communications at any time by utilizing the automated &quot;unsubscribe&quot; link embedded at the bottom of every email sent via Kit, or by sending a direct request to us.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Section 7: Corporate Modifications</h2>
<p>The Company reserves the right to amend this Privacy Policy at any time to align with legislative changes or platform expansions. Updates will be published immediately on this page with a revised effective date. Continued interaction with the platform following updates constitutes your formal acknowledgement of the modified privacy practices.</p>

